From fe30ff04bf3143ea91ec97c9c304956ff233c973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:24:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] crypto: eip93 - queue requests and wait for ring credits

Queue skcipher, AEAD and hash submissions on an ordered worker. Keep
submitting independent requests until the hardware ring or request IDs
are full, then sleep on credits returned by the completion tasklet. A
request larger than the ring resumes as individual descriptors complete.

Use the Crypto API queue backlog contract: accepted requests return
EINPROGRESS, accepted backlog requests return EBUSY and receive an
EINPROGRESS notification when promoted. Requests without MAY_BACKLOG can
be rejected with ENOSPC only when the software queue is full.

Prepare DMA in sleepable worker context, complete preparation failures
once, and drain queued and in-flight operations before stopping
interrupts. This replaces the submission retry sleeps and prevents
ordinary ID exhaustion from aborting a kTLS TX socket.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
